Status: merged (2026-11-18)
Commit: d3d07ad34192759ea4978cfd02250c0270161683

Backport the Venom codegen guard that rejects `==`/`!=` on structs, static
and dynamic arrays and tuples with TypeMismatch, as legacy codegen does,
instead of comparing the two memory pointers (issue #4960). Bytestrings
still compare by hash: that branch returns before the guard.
The unit test calls the pin's `generate_runtime_venom` in place of master's
`generate_venom_runtime`; the rest applies unchanged.

